[Music]  lula is back  at 76 former president louisiana  says he's older wiser and ready to lead  a coalition of center-left parties to  victory in october's presidential  election  i want to tell you that i am willing to  govern brazil 12 years after leaving the  presidency and 12 years we learned a lot  we are able to see what we did for the  country what we did not do and what we  could have done a former car factory  worker lula governed brazil from 2003 to  2010.  as president he was one of the world's  most popular leaders  but after leaving office he was jailed  on corruption charges and barred from  running again  his political fate changed last year  when brazil's supreme court annulled his  trial  since then he has emerged as the most  formidable challenger to the incumbent  jair bolsonaro  i think that corruption is going to be  an issue  because  bolsonaro will make sure that he will  use  the  the the corruption scandal against ruler  but  i think that  after  the  almost four years of bolsonaro  and in  several cases of corruption his  government  this has not  this has changed it's not  it's not  in a weapon that will fire only on one  side  maggie fernandez voted for bolsonaro but  four years on she's disappointed  bolsonaro was elected promising to fight  corruption to reduce public spending and  to adopt business friendly economic  measures he did the opposite he is  wheeling and dealing to win support in  congress something he said he would  never do  there is corruption and the economy is  in shreds  rule is trying to appeal to disappointed  bolsonaro voters by choosing a former  adversary and center-right politician  geraldo alchemy as his vice president  he's also counting on anger at  bolsonaro's denial of the coven 19  pandemic which killed  660 000 brazilians  and his anti-environmental policies  recent polls show lula defeating  bolsonaro political analyst sasha  branchish says rejection more than  approval will play a major role in this  e